      "detail": "Default sampling grid is the TR midpoint (`slice_timing_offset=TR/2`); Nilearn/SPM/FitLins use frame start. Any cross-tool comparison needs `slice_timing_offset=0.0`."
    },
    {
      "scenario": "s01_two_condition_t[small]",
      "axis": "friction",
      "detail": "Drift is opt-in: `fmri_lm` fits no high-pass unless the spec has `drift()`; Nilearn applies a 100 s cosine by default (fmrimod's `drift()` default is SPM's 128 s)."
    },
    {
      "scenario": "s03_parametric_rt[small]",
      "axis": "friction",
      "detail": "Modulators expand per condition, so a pooled RT effect is the sum of per-level slopes (`'trial_type:rt.face + trial_type:rt.house'`); there is no single pooled-modulator spelling."
    },
    {
      "scenario": "s05_fir_shape[small]",
      "axis": "friction",
      "detail": "`hrf(..., basis='fir', nbasis=N)` without `span=` still covers 24 s whatever N is; one bin per scan needs `span=N * tr` (Nilearn's `fir_delays` are in scans)."
    },
    {
      "scenario": "s06_ar1_t[small]",
      "axis": "friction",
      "detail": "AR(1) estimators differ (fmrimod's pooled estimate vs Nilearn's quantised voxelwise AR(1)), so agreement is r\u22480.996 rather than exact. Parity of the AR path itself is tier_a_ar1_prewhitening's job."
    },
    {
      "scenario": "s07_lss_beta_series[small]",
      "axis": "friction",
      "detail": "Single-trial estimation has no image shorthand: unlike `fmri_lm`, `estimate_single_trial_from_dataset` needs an explicit `fmri_dataset(...)` first."
    },
    {
      "scenario": "s09_design_only[small]",
      "axis": "friction",
      "detail": "Column names repeat the term (`trial_type_trial_type.face`, `base_cosine1_block_1`) where Nilearn uses `face`, `drift_1`. Deferred: renaming is a public-contract change (parity receipts, BIDS export)."
    }
  ]
}
